.TH HTGET 1
.SH NAME
htget \- download an HTTP file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B htget
.RI http://HOST[:PORT]/PATH " FILE|-"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolve HOST and retrieve an HTTP body. Use - as FILE to write to stdout.
Content-length, connection-close and chunked framing are supported, with
informational responses and up to five HTTP redirects. Partial socket reads
and writes are handled. An idle read or write times out after 30 seconds.
.PP
For a named file, a temporary file is created in the destination directory.
Only a successful response and complete transfer replace the destination.
HTTP errors, malformed or truncated bodies and interruption preserve an
existing file. Ctrl-C removes the temporary file and returns to the shell.
.PP
Only cleartext http:// is supported. HTTPS/TLS, authentication, cookies and
compressed-content decoding are not implemented. Header lines are limited to
1024 characters and header blocks to 16 KiB. DNS uses /etc/hosts and
/etc/resolv.conf. Saved file lengths count guest C characters, one per octet.
.SH EXAMPLE
htget http://example.com/ /example.html
.SH SEE ALSO
dig(1), host(1), ifconfig(1)
